1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,000
CRAZY (ADJ.): INSANE, ABSURD, MENTALLY UNSOUND,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,680
OR EXCESSIVELY OBSESSED
OR PREOCCUPIED WITH SOMETHING

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,600
(Some people say I’m crazy. )

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,560
(That’s not true. )

5
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,320
You like abstract paintings?

6
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,640
They say you don’t need to think
when you look at abstract art.

7
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,120
You just need to feel—

8
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,120
I’m not into women.

9
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:38,400
I heard your friend was wondering

10
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,600
whether I’m into men or women.

11
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:42,240
So he sent you to find out for him.

12
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:49,040
Well, tell your friend I’m into men.

13
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,720
I’m just not into him.

14
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:03,040
[MANIAC]

15
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,840
(If someone like me is crazy,)
[MANIAC]

16
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:06,680
(then what does that make this guy?)

17
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,360
Why the hell did you call me here?

18
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,840
To do something crazy.

19
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,640
Cheers!

20
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,400
ONE MONTH EARLIER

21
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,280
Another shot?

22
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,400
Easy there.

23
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:38,640
I just got here.

24
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,760
Hey. Why didn’t you just chug it?

25
00:03:43,079 --> 00:03:43,800
I can’t.

26
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,800
Who’s gonna take care of me if I’m drunk?

27
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,720
I’ll take care of you.

28
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:49,120
What number is he in the queue, though?

29
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,000
Hold on.

30
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:57,280
[CAN I COME OVER?]

31
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:57,920
[I SAW YOU THERE.]

32
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:58,640
[MISS YOU.]

33
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,200
[WHERE ARE YOU?]

34
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,520
[CAN I COME OVER?]
[WAITING RIGHT HERE.]

35
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,560
[I SAW YOU THERE.]
[WHY NOT COME OVER AND SAY HI?]

36
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,680
[MISS YOU.]
[MISS YOU MORE.]

37
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,360
Hey, I’m heading back to my table.

38
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:07,920
Be right back.

39
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:08,480
Mhm.

40
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,200
Just a sec.

41
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:12,800
Whoa.

42
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,760
Seriously?

43
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,040
I’ll come back for you.

44
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,000
Cheers!

45
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,280
How have you been?
I haven’t seen you in forever.

46
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,880
Hey, I miss you.

47
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:30,440
See you later. I’ll swing by.

48
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:33,680
There you are.

49
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,680
What a hottie, you asshole.

50
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,880
Took you long enough to get here.

51
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,760
What, you want
a Nobel Friendship Prize or something?

52
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,720
Isn’t it called the Nobel Peace Prize?

53
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,440
Why’d you get this table?

54
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,120
It’s out of sight.

55
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,760
Didn’t you tell them
it was my table when you got here?

56
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,520
Quit complaining.

57
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:53,400
Jo!

58
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,600
Jo, hello.

59
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:55,880
Mhm.

60
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,280
Bro, can I switch to another table?

61
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:59,560
My friend booked us a terrible table.

62
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,360
Why?

63
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,400
It’s not convenient for you
to ogle people from there, huh?

64
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,640
That’s not it.

65
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,720
Come on.

66
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,360
A famous influencer like you
turns heads wherever you go.

67
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,240
Please, bro.

68
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:15,840
It’s so terrible.

69
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,920
The view sucks.

70
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,000
Fine.

71
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:19,800
Thank you.

72
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,440
You came here to look at your dog?

73
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:26,960
Are you nuts?

74
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,320
What? I’m worried about my baby.

75
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:32,760
If you’re that worried,
why the hell did you come here?

76
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:33,680
I had to.

77
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,760
I wanted to see my baby’s Phor Phor.

78
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,960
He told me he’d be here tonight.

79
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:42,440
Who?

80
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,200
This man.

81
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,640
Ah.

82
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:45,480
Dr. PUN.

83
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,600
You know him?

84
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,040
He’s pretty well known.

85
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:53,080
Don’t tell me you and Dr. PUN...

86
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:54,800
Used to...

87
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,840
Used to, my ass!

88
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,280
Stop thinking I’ve hooked up
with everyone in the world.

89
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,120
Dean.

90
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:01,680
Hey.

91
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,560
You’re here too, Hun?

92
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,000
I come here once in a while.

93
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,720
But every time I do, I run into you.

94
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,400
Maybe it’s fate.

95
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,000
Yeah?

96
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,000
- Have you had any drinks yet?
- I have.

97
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:10,840
Not everyone in the world,

98
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,520
but everyone in this club.

99
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,360
Cheers!

100
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,800
Whoo!

101
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,840
That’s Ohm and Boom.

102
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,200
This is my friend, Ten.

103
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,680
He’s an indie kid.

104
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,680
He got us a table all the way in the back.

105
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,040
F*cking horrible.

106
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:30,800
And this is Hun.

107
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,880
He came alone, so I asked him to join us.

108
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:33,600
Is that okay?

109
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,280
Of course.

110
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,520
It’s just the two of us anyway.

111
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,360
Clink.

112
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,520
Cheers!

113
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,440
Just tell me.

114
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:41,760
Out of these three,

115
00:06:42,159 --> 00:06:43,440
who did you have a fling with?

116
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,240
All of them.

117
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,240
What?!

118
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,480
And you brought them all to the same table?

119
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,800
Ohm and Boom are close now
because I introduced them.

120
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,880
And Hun...

121
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,480
I’m sure he’ll get close to them too.

122
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,800
Are you crazy?

123
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,640
Dean, I got you a new table.

124
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,560
Oops. Sorry, bro.

125
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,520
You were gone for so long.

126
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,160
I thought you couldn’t find me another table,

127
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,320
so I joined my friends here instead.

128
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:06,240
You always manage just fine without me.

129
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,800
Aw, I’m sorry, Jo.

130
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:10,240
Here. Let me pour you a drink.

131
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,280
Come on!

132
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,200
Cheers!

133
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,720
Whoo!

134
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,480
Are you drunk yet?

135
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:51,560
Hey.

136
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:53,680
Dean.

137
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:55,720
Hi, Dr. PUN.

138
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,920
I didn’t know you liked it here.

139
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:01,280
I don’t come here often,
but my friend asked me to come tonight.

140
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,520
You came with friends?

141
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,040
That’s right.

142
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:10,280
This is Ten, my close friend.

143
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,160
You two have met before, right?

144
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,400
Yeah?

145
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:20,440
Today.

146
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:22,760
This afternoon.

147
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,760
At your clinic.

148
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:27,920
Ah!

149
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,280
You’re Mademoiselle’s dad?

150
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,679
I’m sorry. It’s dark in here.

151
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,840
I couldn’t really see you.

152
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,679
And my brain’s a little fuzzy today.

153
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:40,280
How embarrassing.

154
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:42,400
Have you got a table, PUN?

155
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,120
If not, you can join us.

156
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:44,960
It’s alright.

157
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,760
I came with a friend. Would you excuse me?

158
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:49,920
Sure.

159
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:11,160
[HI. I LIKE YOUR WORK.]

160
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:15,920
[THANK YOU.]

161
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:20,720
[IS THIS YOU? YOU’RE CUTE.]

162
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:32,400
Sorry.

163
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,160
Did I keep you waiting?

164
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,400
Don’t answer that.

165
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,200
Whatever you want to yell at me for,
just keep it to yourself.

166
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,240
It was the traffic. I’m sorry.

167
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,520
Why do you look so annoyed?

168
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,280
I should’ve agreed to
show my face in that interview.

169
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,120
It was a huge mistake.

170
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:56,960
Why?

171
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:01,320
You’re a rising artist who looks like a TV star.

172
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,360
Isn’t that a good thing?

173
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:06,280
If it helps me land more opportunities
or get more work,

174
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,160
then sure, it’s a good thing.

175
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:11,520
But all I get are people trying to flirt with me.

176
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,200
It’s annoying.

177
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,320
Wow.

178
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:20,400
If that came from anyone else,
it’d sound so obnoxious.

179
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,480
I don’t want to deal with people,

180
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:24,720
and I don’t want them bothering me.

181
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:25,880
That’s all.

182
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,640
Turn to your right.

183
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,680
That’s Dean.

184
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,880
From ‘Everydeanlive’ channel.

185
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,240
I don’t know him.

186
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,600
What? How can you not know him?

187
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,280
He’s famous.

188
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:50,880
He has, like, a million followers.

189
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,080
I only pay attention to useful stuff.

190
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,640
Don’t worry, Ten.

191
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,440
I’m going to take you there
to hit on Dr. PUN.

192
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,080
Where’s Ten?

193
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:31,440
Who’s Ten again?

194
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,000
Ten!

195
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:53,760
Argh!

196
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:55,120
Gosh.

197
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:58,840
Ten!

198
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,640
Hey. Why are you whining?

199
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,960
My baby just came in to say hi.

200
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,440
Mademoiselle, sweetheart.

201
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,560
Don’t get too close to him.
He reeks of booze.

202
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,320
Checking up on your catches
from last night, huh?

203
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,200
Off you go, honey.

204
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,400
Did you bail on someone who’s supposed to
crash at your place last night?

205
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,200
That’s why you had to crash at mine instead.

206
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,080
No one.

207
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,720
I just forgot my house key.

208
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,440
And I never bail on anyone.

209
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:35,640
I only get bailed on by people.

210
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:37,480
Especially you.

211
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,000
It wasn’t even midnight,
and you were already gone.

212
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:40,920
Asshole.

213
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,280
What?

214
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,320
I didn’t want my baby sleeping alone.

215
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:51,760
Oh, yeah?

216
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:56,360
It had nothing to do
with Dr. PUN ignoring you?

217
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:57,600
Hey.

218
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:58,760
What?

219
00:12:58,880 --> 00:12:59,760
What exactly is the deal between you two?

220
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,200
Huh?

221
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,160
Have you actually ever talked to him?

222
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,200
Yes, I really have.

223
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:06,520
Yeah?

224
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:07,840
Yes.

225
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:08,720
Talked about what?

226
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,720
I… took Mademoiselle
to his clinic for treatment.

227
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,680
We talked while
he was checking on my baby.

228
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:22,840
And then he told you
he was going to the club?

229
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,280
Hm?

230
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,560
I overheard him saying it on the phone.

231
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,840
I knew it, you dipshit.

232
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,760
You were his customer, dude.

233
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:37,760
Damn it.

234
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,800
But I really like him.

235
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:44,400
I think about him when I wake up.

236
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:47,160
When I sleep, I dream about him, my friend.

237
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:50,160
I’ve never felt this way about anyone before.

238
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:56,040
I can’t help you with that.

239
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,240
He has a boyfriend.

240
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:58,080
What boyfriend?

241
00:13:58,440 --> 00:13:59,360
He doesn’t.

242
00:13:59,400 --> 00:13:59,800
What?

243
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,120
The guy who came with him last night.

244
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,320
Wasn’t that his boyfriend?

245
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:31,960
Don’t worry.

246
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,520
Just make sure this baby takes
the medication and follow my advice.

247
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,240
Recovery should be quick.

248
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,640
Sure. Thank you, Doctor.

249
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,240
Of course.

250
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,400
Bye-bye.

251
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,720
Get some rest, little one.

252
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,160
See you later.

253
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,120
Hello.

254
00:14:56,240 --> 00:15:00,640
Could you write down 97/42
and put it up in front of the building, please?

255
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:22,760
Yeah?

256
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,600
(Hi. You awake?)

257
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:25,880
Of course I am.

258
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,200
It’s noon.

259
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,040
How was I supposed to know?

260
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:29,920
You went wild last night.

261
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,600
(I went ‘wild’ last night?)

262
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,800
I’ve got a briefing with the author tonight.

263
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,880
So I’m just sketching out
the character designs now.

264
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:40,120
I ordered food for you. It’s downstairs.

265
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:42,760
Don’t forget to come down and get it.

266
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,440
Hey.

267
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:49,200
Will you stop treating me like I’m a kid?

268
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:50,680
I was ordering mine,

269
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:53,080
and there was a promotion,
so I got one for you too.

270
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,400
It’s from your favorite place.

271
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:05,720
Fine.

272
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,680
(The thing is, those two are friends.)

273
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,280
(Dr. PUN secretly has a crush on his friend.)

274
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,800
And how do you know so much about him?

275
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,120
Yeah, whatever. I just do.

276
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:48,320
Dr. PUN has had a thing
for his friend Moth for ages,

277
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:52,280
but he’s never had the guts to confess.

278
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,080
Why?

279
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,920
Because Moth is crazy.

280
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,040
Crazy?

281
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:01,600
How?

282
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:11,000
(The second someone hits on him,
he turns into a total jerk.)

283
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,760
The gent from that table
sent this over for you.

284
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:21,800
I’m sorry. I have diabetes.

285
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:29,240
(The moment anyone gets romantic with him,
he cuts them out of his life.)

286
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,640
There’s no one in the world
harder to hit on…

287
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,360
than Moth.

288
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:43,600
Dr. PUN knows if
he confesses his feelings to Moth,

289
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:46,080
he’ll get cut off immediately.

290
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,600
That’s why he keeps his feelings to himself.

291
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:53,440
And if things keep going like this,

292
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,560
I’ll never get my chance.

293
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,480
Yeah, totally crazy.

294
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,080
Right?

295
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,840
I didn’t know someone like Moth existed.

296
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,720
I wasn’t talking about him.

297
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,000
I meant you.

298
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:04,560
Damn you.

299
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,600
You’ve got quite an imagination.

300
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:10,040
Stop being delusional
and hurry up and edit my video.

301
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:11,800
I have to send the first draft
to my client tomorrow.

302
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:13,360
Yeah.

303
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:16,320
And before you go digging into his backstory,

304
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:21,240
does Dr. PUN even know you exist?

305
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,240
Mm.

306
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:25,800
He’s up there.

307
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:29,480
A guy from down here like me
doesn’t stand a chance.

308
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,160
No, dude.

309
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,160
That’s not what I meant.

310
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:48,960
But if you like him, go after him.

311
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,120
Instead of talking about him all day.

312
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:03,920
Do you really think
I have a chance of winning Dr. PUN’s heart?

313
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:04,960
Of course you do.

314
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,960
Anything can happen in this world.

315
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,200
But you can’t just sit around
waiting for your chance.

316
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:12,040
You have to go out and find it.

317
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:21,200
But if he won’t open up to me, that’ll be hard.

318
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,040
Holy shit.

319
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,720
I figured it out.

320
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,240
I’m going to pursue Dr. PUN.

321
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,760
But I need you to go after Moth.

322
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,760
I’ve read your manuscript, Mr. Phol.

323
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,160
So I decided to draw a few
character designs for you to take a look at.

324
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,920
- The characters are…
- This isn’t a work pitch.

325
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,680
I’ve been following your work, Mr. Moth.

326
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:11,480
No matter what, I’m confident you’re
the right person to illustrate my project.

327
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:13,960
Ah.

328
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:18,840
You said you wanted to talk, so I thought...

329
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,600
I just wanted to get to know you.

330
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:25,320
Because if we work together,
we could be collaborating for years.

331
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,480
If this project becomes successful.

332
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,720
I’m sorry. I didn’t mean...

333
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:33,880
I’m sure it’ll be successful.

334
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,280
So, do you have a partner?

335
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,600
And you just walked away from him like that?

336
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:57,000
Damn straight.

337
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,480
Work, my ass.

338
00:20:58,840 --> 00:20:59,960
All he asked was, “Do you have a partner?”

339
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,240
and “What’s your type?”

340
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:02,440
Is he insane?

341
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:04,440
(You don’t want to work with him anymore?)

342
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:06,480
Of course I do.

343
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:09,080
He comes up with such creative stories.

344
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:12,880
The moment I found out he was looking for
a new illustrator, I wanted the job.

345
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:15,400
But in the end, you dumped him.

346
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:19,640
I just want to work. Nothing else.

347
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:22,640
(Don’t you think that’s a wasted opportunity?)

348
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:26,920
A wasted opportunity?

349
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:31,000
With some books,
if you already know how they end,

350
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,240
there’s no point
wasting your time reading them.

351
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:41,880
I want a drink.

352
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:44,480
Are you free tonight?

353
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,080
I’m going to a doctor friend’s wedding.

354
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:59,160
But I can leave early and come see you.

355
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,320
Hey, it’s okay.

356
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,040
Go to your friend’s thing.

357
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:07,560
But I...

358
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:08,080
(Bye.)

359
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:41,640
Hey, Dean.

360
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:42,800
Did you book a table tonight?

361
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:43,560
No, bro.

362
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,440
I’ll get one later.

363
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:46,760
Right. It shouldn’t be a problem for you.

364
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,280
Please, dude.

365
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,040
Go hit on Moth for me.

366
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:14,520
What kind of crazy shit
are you talking about?

367
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:15,640
Cut the nonsense.

368
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:17,920
I’m not talking nonsense.

369
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:23,240
The only way to get Dr. PUN
to open up to me...

370
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:26,160
is to make him get over Moth.

371
00:23:26,560 --> 00:23:26,920
Mhm.

372
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,680
And that can only happen

373
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,120
if Moth starts seeing someone.

374
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,080
And why does that someone have to be me?

375
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:40,800
Well, a maniac like Moth
is perfect for a maniac like you.

376
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,080
Perfect match.

377
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:44,200
Me?

378
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,080
I’m a maniac?

379
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,520
Why?

380
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,400
What, are you scared
you can’t win him over?

381
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:56,360
Guess we’re about to find out
you’re not as charming as you think.

382
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,320
I’m never scared, Ten.

383
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,960
Is this seat taken?

384
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,000
No,

385
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:19,760
but it’s reserved.

386
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:22,520
Reserved for your partner?

387
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:28,680
I’m kidding.

388
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,840
You’re Dr. PUN’s friend, right?

389
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,280
I saw you here with him the other night.

390
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:35,280
I’m Dean.

391
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,240
PUN’s not coming tonight.

392
00:24:45,080 --> 00:24:47,680
If you’re here to hit on him,
just DM him on Insta.

393
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:55,120
I don’t have his Insta,

394
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:58,200
and I’m not hitting on him.

395
00:24:59,440 --> 00:25:00,240
We just know each other.

396
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:03,680
I’m Dean.

397
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:04,480
I know.

398
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:06,880
You already told me.

399
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:09,240
Aren’t you going to tell me your name?

400
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,560
The seat’s reserved, so no one sits here.

401
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:13,520
Did you come here alone?

402
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:22,880
Must be lonely.

403
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,600
You know who’s lonely?

404
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:31,240
Someone who tries to chat up a stranger.

405
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:34,560
Okay.

406
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:35,520
Then…

407
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:38,000
Have fun.

408
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:43,880
Hey! I thought you looked familiar.

409
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,400
Whoa. I thought you’d forgotten about me.

410
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,440
How could I forget you?

411
00:25:47,720 --> 00:25:48,960
Who did you come with?

412
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:49,920
No one.

413
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:52,280
I don’t have a table yet. Can I join you?

414
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,040
Why did you tell me
to check out that guy, Dean?

415
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Why do you ask?

416
00:26:07,160 --> 00:26:07,760
You like him?

417
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:08,480
Don’t be funny.

418
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:10,600
I’m just curious.

419
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:12,040
So why did you tell me to look at him?

420
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:14,240
Remember Ong?

421
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:15,800
From Class 4 back in high school?

422
00:26:16,840 --> 00:26:17,320
Mm-hm.

423
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:20,880
And Thames, that friend
from my faculty I introduced you to?

424
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:22,920
The name rings a bell.

425
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:24,440
I just can’t remember his face.

426
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:27,920
Mark, the guy who designed my clinic.

427
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,960
And James, my peer mentee.

428
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Now none of that rings a bell.

429
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:33,040
Why are you throwing
all these names at me?

430
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:34,720
Here’s the thing.

431
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:39,600
Everyone I just mentioned
had a fling with Dean.

432
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,320
And all at the same time.

433
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:59,040
Whoo!

434
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:05,080
(Have fun.)

435
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,320
[TELL ME WHEN YOU GET HOME.]

436
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,720
[I’M WORRIED.]

437
00:27:57,680 --> 00:27:58,560
You smell nice.

438
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:23,800
Move.

439
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:25,440
How cute.

440
00:28:29,760 --> 00:28:31,720
Can I get your Insta?

441
00:28:33,520 --> 00:28:34,280
Moth.

442
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:40,160
You already know my account.

443
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,200
Why ask?

444
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:44,240
I want you to give it to me.

445
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:46,720
What do you want it for?

446
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,160
To talk.

447
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:50,360
To snoop.

448
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:54,320
To flirt.

449
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:01,520
Can I hit on you?

450
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:22,560
[I’M NOT GOING TO BED
UNTIL YOU’RE HOME.]

451
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:38,080
If you dare, you can try.

452
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:01,520
Another Old Fashioned, please.

453
00:30:01,520 --> 00:30:02,640
But make it stronger.

454
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,840
We need to clear things up.

455
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:26,840
Clear what up?

456
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:28,440
Are you drunk?

457
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:30,040
Why did you just disappear?

458
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:31,840
And why did you suddenly show up today?

459
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:32,960
I didn’t disappear.

460
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:34,720
I’m still following you on IG.

461
00:30:34,720 --> 00:30:35,800
I still like your Stories.

462
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,240
But whenever I asked you out,
you never said yes.

463
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:38,240
Because I wasn’t available.

464
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:39,440
Not available, or just not lonely?

465
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:40,720
So you’re lonely tonight?

466
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,520
Is that why you came?

467
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,000
What am I to you, you jerk?

468
00:30:43,320 --> 00:30:44,440
Do you think I don’t have feelings?

469
00:30:46,600 --> 00:30:47,160
Hold on.

470
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,280
We never agreed on what we were.

471
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:53,400
If we can’t even be friends in the end,

472
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:55,760
then let’s just stop talking altogether.

473
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:55,800
So you like to drink alone...

474
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:57,640
and dance alone too?

475
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:34,760
You’re drunk.

476
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:36,240
Why?

477
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:38,080
Can’t I get drunk?

478
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:39,320
Sure, you can.

479
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:45,680
You can do whatever you want.

480
00:32:58,000 --> 00:32:58,640
I’m going home.

481
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:07,080
Wait.

482
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:08,160
How are you getting home?

483
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:08,600
I’m booking a ride.

484
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:10,600
Want me to take you home?

485
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:11,760
No.

486
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:14,760
Sure you can get home safely on your own?

487
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:19,160
I’m not taking you to my place.

488
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:21,320
And I never plan on going to yours.

489
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:25,360
So don’t waste your time pestering me.

490
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,200
Do you put your walls up around everyone?

491
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,280
Or just me?

492
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:45,920
I’m just asking.

493
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:48,040
Are you sure you can
get home on your own?

494
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:49,960
Mhm.

495
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:54,680
Well then, get home safe.

496
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:01,240
Please.

497
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:09,000
I’ll send you flirty messages on IG.

498
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,680
[TELL ME WHEN YOU GET HOME.]
[I’M WORRIED]

499
00:35:01,680 --> 00:35:03,000
[I’M NOT GOING TO BED
UNTIL YOU’RE HOME.]

500
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:05,320
[I’M HOME.]

501
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:10,640
[OKAY. GOOD NIGHT THEN.]

502
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:57,080
(It’s a tee, not a tease.
Don’t forget to purchase.)

503
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:14,680
[STILL ON FOR TONIGHT?]
[DID YOU LEAVE?]

504
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:16,080
[WHERE ARE YOU?]
[HAVE YOU FORGOTTEN ABOUT ME?]

505
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:17,000
[I STILL MISS YOU.]

506
00:36:56,320 --> 00:37:01,640
[GOOD NIGHT.]

507
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,800
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

508
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:22,840
[ARE YOU UP?]

509
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:24,720
[YOU NEVER REPLY TO ME.]

510
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:27,680
[WERE YOU IN THAT CLUB LAST NIGHT?]

511
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:32,000
[GOOD NIGHT.]

512
00:37:38,960 --> 00:37:44,960
[GOOD NIGHT.]

513
00:37:50,440 --> 00:37:51,000
Yeah?

514
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:52,920
(I’m booking a table tonight.)

515
00:37:53,840 --> 00:37:54,520
What for?

516
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,640
To celebrate your birthday.

517
00:37:57,600 --> 00:37:59,680
(But my birthday’s in two days.)

518
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:06,360
Don’t forget your own rule.

519
00:38:06,440 --> 00:38:09,920
(You always go
full introvert on your birthday.)

520
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,760
(So if I’m throwing you a party,
I have to do it early.)

521
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:13,160
But...

522
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,040
(No buts.)

523
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:15,920
It’s that mala place you like.

524
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:17,720
See you at eight.

525
00:38:40,640 --> 00:38:41,800
Happy birthday.

526
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:44,840
Wow.

527
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:46,480
Thank you.

528
00:38:49,680 --> 00:38:50,760
Without you,

529
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:55,000
someone horrible like me
wouldn’t have any close friends left.

530
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,120
I don’t want to lose you.

531
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:03,440
Sooner or later, you’ll have a partner,

532
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,320
and a friend like me
will become less important.

533
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:13,680
I won’t have a partner.

534
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:16,320
No way.

535
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,080
You, on the other hand...

536
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:19,880
You’re a good person.

537
00:39:20,680 --> 00:39:22,960
One day, someone good
will come into your life.

538
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:27,920
And then I’ll become less important to you.

539
00:39:30,880 --> 00:39:31,520
No.

540
00:39:32,720 --> 00:39:34,760
You’ll never mean any less to me.

541
00:39:52,360 --> 00:39:53,640
Happy birthday.

542
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:58,920
I hope this year is kind to you.

543
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,920
I hope you get to chase your dreams.

544
00:40:02,280 --> 00:40:04,480
Have your own proper exhibition.

545
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:06,960
And most importantly,

546
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:13,600
I hope you’re lucky in game
and lucky in love.

547
00:40:38,680 --> 00:40:39,160
Hello.

548
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:40,880
(Are you free tonight?)

549
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,640
Can we meet at the same club?)

550
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:44,760
Of course.

551
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:47,560
Then can you book a table for three?

552
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:52,000
You, me, and my friend PUN.

553
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:53,600
Sure.

554
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,280
I’ll bring a friend too.

555
00:40:55,680 --> 00:40:56,440
Make it four.

556
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:00,400
Okay?

557
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:21,120
- You guys close enough
to ask each other to hang out?

558
00:41:21,760 --> 00:41:24,480
- I’m giving you an opening.
Find a chance to talk to Dr. PUN.

559
00:41:24,480 --> 00:41:27,440
- Are you okay with me
getting close to Dean?

560
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:31,480
- You’re not thinking of getting
serious with him anyway, right?

561
00:41:31,640 --> 00:41:34,960
- You asked me to come,
and now you’re ditching me just like that?

562
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,480
- Didn’t you say you wanted to hit on me?

563
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:39,360
- Well, I’m right here for you to hit on.

564
00:41:44,240 --> 00:41:47,000
- I’m glad I got to know you.
